Traveling to High Hrothgar requires scaling the "[[Skyrim:Climb the Steps|7,000 steps]]" from [[Skyrim:Ivarstead|Ivarstead]]. On the way up to High Hrothgar there will be at least one [[Skyrim:Frost Troll|frost troll]] on the path regardless of your level (though you can avoid fighting it), and you will potentially encounter several more cold-themed enemies like [[Skyrim:Snow Bear|snow bears]] and [[Skyrim:Ice Wraith|ice wraiths]]. In addition to enemy encounters, a few travelers will be seen on the way to the top - pilgrims who are exploring and reading the wisdom etched on the [[#Etched Tablets|ancient tablets]]. Reading all of the tablets grants the [[Skyrim:Voice of the Sky|Voice of the Sky]] effect for 24 hours, which prevents animals from either attacking or fleeing from you; the tablets do not need to be read in numerical order to obtain this effect.

